As I continued to build out the features, the code structure started to get disjoined and I wanted to note down some changes I need to make:

- I need to group the components into the modes more cleanly. 
    - The design and implementation components are in their own folder but the implementation is in the root. This is mainly because I have actually defined more about the application strucutre as I was exploring and I didn't take the time to make changes to the folder structure to reflect this. I am also sharing components between the modes, like the behavioral control graph, I don't want to do this, I want dedicated components per mode.

- I need to separate the stores into slices in a cleaner way
    - Right now when I select the behavior in the behavioral control graph in the design mode, it is using the thunk in the root store. Then when I deselect a behavior in design mode, I am manually clearing the transform output log, the primitive etc (because no active behavior is present). If I create a separate selector for the design mode, I can cleanly manage the state in the design thunk and simplify my life. 

- Update the debugging UI to highlight the difference with execution versus design debugging interfaces
    - I am using the same user interface for the implementation debugging and the design debugging, this is not correct.
    - The design trace's observed environment is just what the engine calcluated, I am essentially recalculating and verifying that the output is the same (which it always will be)
    - There is nothign inherently wrong with this, its just misleading to the end user, so I will make that clear.
    - The UI's themselves will evolve soon.

- I need to clean up the participant and invariant components.
    - I've fully moved away from the participants and the invariant components in favour of the scripting language. So I need to remove those.

- I need to url arguments for sepecific traces or behaviors and then I need to add keybaord shortcuts for moving between the modes.
    - The reason for the traces or behavior url args is because it will allow me to load the UI into a sepcific state.
    - Moving between nodes is because it will help me see the results of my executions.

- Add behavioral control graph to the debug view and allow a visualization of which node is being inspected using the position from the design trace.
    - This one is relavtivel simply, I just want to visualize where I am in the atomic design path on top of the behavioral control graph.

- All the toolbars should share the same style sheet.
    - This is part of a bigger change that I mentioned a while back where I am defining style sheets on the fly and this one will probably wait until much later when I create my component library. 

Essentially, since I established these three modes, I haven't taken the time to make changes to the code structure to reflect these changes. SO I am leaving a note here for myself to fix it and to be consistent with my naming for the design, implementation and debugging modes.

Luckily, none of these changes are very difficult and once I dedicate a day to this, I will be able to move it forward cleanly.